                <pb facs="0345" n="245" xml:id="pg245"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.00/3366: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Dodd</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-08-21T10:00:00+01:00">August 21, 1934—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 21—9:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>171. In an appeal to the National Socialists and German people, Chancellor
                    observes that with Sunday’s plebiscite victory and the whole administration in
                    National Socialist hands 15 years struggle after power has closed; the present
                    task is to strengthen unity and win the last remnant of people for National
                    Socialist ideas and doctrines in a determined ingenious and persevering
                    campaign; decisions for execution of this action have already been taken and
                    will be carried out with National Socialist rapidity and thoroughness.</p>
                <p>Hitler also publicly thanked the Reichswehr for its oath of allegiance and again
                    upheld its inviolability as the sole bearer of arms in the Nation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dodd</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
